Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[" Section 5.2", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"dc5187ff-adf2-4894-afc3-e0976637a78f"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["  Algae Blooms",
 FontWeight->"Bold"]], "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"07d51e3f-c816-42a0-b297-160f05fd838e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{" ", 
  RowBox[{"Remove", "[", "\"\<Global`*\>\"", " ", "]"}]}]], "InputOnly",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.398494066793*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1478]:=",ExpressionUUID->"07288eed-c1a4-479f-b8d5-ec82c45ccb19"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[" Introduction:", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"3c8d145b-a612-4aaa-ab67-5bf9494821a3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "An accumulation of nutrients favorable to the growth of certain tiny marine \
organisms called phytoplankton stimulates their rapid reproduction in the \
ocean.  These plankton blooms appear as patches on the surface of the water.  \
\n\nOutside a given patch the conditions for growth are unfavorable and so \
none takes place.\n\nThe plankton are swept to and fro by wave action and the \
wind, and so the flux within an island-like patch may be considered as \
diffusion.\n\nThis suggests that we generate a conservation model based on \
diffusion.\n\nHowever, there is additional flux out of the full patch as some \
algae gets carried beyond the boundaries of the patch and is lost.\n\nHowever \
there is an internal source term corresponding to reproduction which \
constantly adds to the overall population.\n\nThe trade-off between \
reproduction and eventual lost at the boundary's edge means that there must \
be a minimal size for a patch if the population is not to die out.  Diffusion \
within a small enough environment will usually out strip the ability of the \
remaining plankton to provide new recruits who can replace those lost by \
dispersion at the outer boundaries.\n\nAlthough the ocean surface is \
two-dimensional, ",
 StyleBox["we assume that the plankton density is homogeneous in one of the \
two dimensions and varies only along the remaining x-coordinate",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 ".  This assumption will reduce the two-dimensional problem to a \
one-dimensional problem, which is necessary at our current stage of \
mathematical development.\n\nOur problem is to find the minimum length L of a \
patch (i.e. in a one-dimensional slice of the ocean surface) that permits a \
plankton bloom to occur.\n"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9b4821f2-71f3-4219-8272-5a87b00947a5"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[" Model Development:", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"bc03f842-ddc1-4c10-a512-c90d01cea5d2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Our basic dependent variable  \[Rho][x,t]  will be the local density of the \
plankton bloom at location x and time t.\n\nThe primary mechanism for flux \
within a patch is diffusion and not advection.  Therefore our model for \
internal flux is:\n\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["q", "Diffusion"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "367a0d30-e6b9-4169-a466-3aa3b003cd59"],
 "  =  - \[Nu]   ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x"], 
    RowBox[{"(", "\[Rho]", ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "7037081a-2bda-4a8c-8ff7-9bd85807bc73"],
 "\n\t\nFinally, our only source term is the net rate of population increase \
due to reproduction:\n\t\n\tk[x,t]\n\t\nThus, our model for the internal \
behavior of a patch reduces to a conservation PDE with diffusion flux and a \
source term:\n\n \t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{" ", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "t"], 
     RowBox[{"(", " ", "\[Rho]", " ", ")"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"ac6f358e-21b5-41f7-a2bf-d14da8f01b77"],
 "  =   \[Nu] ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{" ", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "xx"], 
     RowBox[{"(", " ", 
      FormBox[
       RowBox[{"\[Rho]", ")"}],
       TraditionalForm], " "}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "ba2edcf9-b0c3-48aa-b0c6-7dfd8b6b5e4e"],
 "  +  k"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7387c5ea-5d02-4ac5-85b1-cddcee04ab55"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[" Source Term:", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"279227c9-c91a-4e8a-a245-900494818b29"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We now need to develop a model for the net rate of population (i.e. \
density) growth.  The examples developed in previous chapters offer two \
possible models:\n\nUnlimited population growth.  Which can be expressed as:\n\
\n\tk[x,t]  =  r \[Rho][x,t]\n\nLogistic population growth.  Which can be \
expressed as:\n\n\tk[x,t]  =  r \[Rho][x,t] (1  -  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox[
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "[", 
      RowBox[{"x", ",", "t"}], "]"}], "k"],
    FontSize->16,
    FontWeight->"Bold"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "db54b52f-713f-4ac4-9368-0d9b4313e817"],
 ")"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c05dd0a7-ba45-49c2-a805-0085b6fb5f42"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[" Unlimited Growth Model:", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"ab0c34fe-a41f-4353-b545-d15f486cf6c6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "If we use unlimited growth for our source term, then be PDE model becomes:\n\
\n \t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{" ", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "t"], 
     RowBox[{"(", " ", "\[Rho]", " ", ")"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"551e8aef-cb16-43de-b108-e18e634642fd"],
 "  =   \[Nu] ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{" ", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "xx"], 
     RowBox[{"(", " ", 
      FormBox[
       RowBox[{"\[Rho]", ")"}],
       TraditionalForm], " "}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "644bc59b-3f2c-4953-8d04-587f5ed259f5"],
 "  +  r \[Rho]\n \t\nThe analysis for this model can proceed along two \
different lines:\n\n\tLooking for steady state solutions.\n\tLooking for \
non-equilibrium solutions."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"76eeed82-b8a5-421c-8938-f87f9f01cc6b"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
 Steady state solutions:
\
\>", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.465151465114111*^9, 
  3.465151470287012*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e56a10ec-5626-4941-a247-\
15422b2fc558"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "First, let's look at the behavior of steady state solutions.  For this \
case:\n\n \t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{" ", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "t"], 
     RowBox[{"(", " ", "\[Rho]", " ", ")"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"ace467ed-76d1-42ef-b3eb-10c074224d95"],
 "  =  0\n \t\nThus, the PDE reduces to an ODE:\n\n \t\[Nu] ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{" ", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "xx"], 
     RowBox[{"(", " ", 
      FormBox[
       RowBox[{"\[Rho]", ")"}],
       TraditionalForm], " "}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "bd9d20ba-bc67-44eb-a807-31c2b11589bc"],
 "  +  r \[Rho]  =  0\n \t"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ad1460b1-691d-4727-837e-a004c2674830"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"DSolve", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\[Nu]", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "'"}], "'"}], "[", "x", "]"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
     RowBox[{"r", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "[", "x", "]"}]}]}], "==", "0"}], ",", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "[", "x", "]"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", "x"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]",
   "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398494247749*^9, 3.3984942599049997`*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1479]:=",ExpressionUUID->"581aebe0-78eb-42b6-9687-84d4f922a738"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
 Fixed boundary conditions:
\
\>", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.465151471521632*^9},ExpressionUUID->"47b12e21-43bc-4eed-85cb-\
849a8421b1b8"],

Cell["\<\
In order to further understand the behavior of the steady state solutions, we \
need to apply the conditions that exist at the boundary of our algae bloom.  \
A reasonable assumption is that the plankton density reduces to 0 at the \
outer edges.  Thus:

\t\[Rho][0]  =  0
\t\[Rho][L]  =  0
\t\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0948da54-8d01-4eaf-9a0a-261116d26d8a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"DSolve", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"\[Nu]", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         SuperscriptBox[
          SuperscriptBox["\[Rho]", "\[Prime]",
           MultilineFunction->None], "\[Prime]",
          MultilineFunction->None], "[", "x", "]"}]}], "+", 
       RowBox[{"r", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "[", "x", "]"}]}]}], "\[Equal]", "0"}], ",", 
     "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "[", "0", "]"}], "\[Equal]", "0"}], ",", 
     "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "[", "L", "]"}], "\[Equal]", "0"}]}], 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "[", "x", "]"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", "x"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]",
   "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398494270592*^9, 3.398494289889*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1480]:=",ExpressionUUID->"56c7d64f-ba6d-4ebb-8aec-aea95f22119e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Thus, one solution to the steady state problem starting from a value of 0 \
and returning to a value of 0 is:\n\n\t\[Rho][x]\[Rule]0\n\nHowever, we can \
try to find other ",
 StyleBox["nonzero",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " solutions:\n\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "[", "x", "]"}], "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"C", "[", "1", "]"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
      FractionBox[
       RowBox[{
        SqrtBox["r"], " ", "x"}], 
       SqrtBox["\[Nu]"]], "]"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->"TraditionalForm",ExpressionUUID->
  "6b077245-9e99-404d-9617-c606d418f178"],
 "\n\nBut this solution only works with the following constraint:\n\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
     FractionBox[
      RowBox[{"L", " ", 
       SqrtBox["r"]}], 
      SqrtBox["\[Nu]"]], "]"}], "\[Equal]", "0"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->"TraditionalForm",ExpressionUUID->
  "482dafb7-4c6b-4a49-b059-6885c6bcdb9e"],
 "\n\nConsider solving for acceptable values of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["L", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->"TraditionalForm",ExpressionUUID->
  "25fb3d41-0502-4dc5-a4bd-d29cdfb8b3e7"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.7504237939025774`*^9, 3.7504238253457212`*^9}, {
  3.7504240382260075`*^9, 
  3.7504241569488783`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"bf88e72d-ef3f-420e-b1e2-\
482e5df31e15"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Solve", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
     FractionBox[
      RowBox[{"L", " ", 
       SqrtBox["r"]}], 
      SqrtBox["\[Nu]"]], "]"}], "\[Equal]", "0"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]",
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", "L"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.39849432581*^9, 3.398494337617*^9}, 
   3.750423946716857*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1481]:=",ExpressionUUID->"a7688b82-5764-457b-b34b-104520419c6f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Mathematica indicates that there is the possibility of many other solutions \
other than ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"L", "\[Rule]", "0"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "dc56ef9e-46d2-4414-aaaf-15c8a82511e1"],
 ".\nIf we desire the smallest solution (other than the zero solution), then \
this corresponds to a value of:\n\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"L", "\[Rule]", 
     FractionBox[
      RowBox[{
       SqrtBox["\[Nu]"], " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "+", 
         RowBox[{"2", " ", "\[Pi]", " ", 
          RowBox[{"C", "[", "1", "]"}]}]}], ")"}]}], 
      SqrtBox["r"]]}], " ", "=", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     FractionBox[
      RowBox[{
       SqrtBox["\[Nu]"], " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "+", 
         RowBox[{"2", " ", "\[Pi]", "*", "0"}]}], ")"}]}], 
      SqrtBox["r"]], "=", " ", 
     FractionBox[
      RowBox[{
       SqrtBox["\[Nu]"], " ", "\[Pi]"}], 
      SqrtBox["r"]]}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->"TraditionalForm",ExpressionUUID->
  "f2714a7d-3f86-4284-b631-4f2a5c3a31ad"],
 "\n"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.750424267746957*^9, 
  3.750424378737055*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"d747c4ab-e701-451a-a8e9-\
8fa7beb39b5c"],

Cell["\<\
This value of L represents the smallest steady state size of the plankton \
bloom using these boundary conditions and the unlimited population model.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"57d1d3ce-6936-4313-b473-4445a90d6800"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
 Flux boundary conditions:
\
\>", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.465151473209467*^9},ExpressionUUID->"a939793e-6334-417b-80d0-\
2583d8653ac2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "However, the above fixed boundary conditions may not be reasonable for our \
plankton bloom.  A more reasonable boundary condition would incorporate the \
loss of plankton on the outer boundary.  After some thought, it might be \
reasonable to assume that the loss (i.e. flux) of plankton at the outer edge \
should depend on:\n\t 1:  Flux from boundary to the outside.\n\t 2:  Flux \
from inside to the boundary.\nBoth of the above fluxes must be equal.\nFor \
\"1\", assume that the flux from the boundary to the outside is proportional \
to the density at that boundary location (i.e. the thicker the plankton at \
the outer edge the more likely it is to break off and float away).  \nThus, \
the relationship between the flux from the boundary to the outside and the \
density at the boundary becomes:\n\n\tq[0,t]   \[Alpha]  - \[Rho][0,t]\t (the \
flux out is right to left, i.e. negative flux)\n\tq[L,t]   \[Alpha]  \
\[Rho][L,t]\t (the flux out is left to right, i.e. positive flux)\n\nFor \
\"2\", assume that the flux from the inside to the boundary is negatively \
proportional to the density gradient (i.e. the shorter the interval over \
which the density drops near the boundary, the faster the inside material is \
transferred to the boundary).  \nThus, the relationship between the flux from \
the inside to the boundary and the density gradient just inside the boundary \
becomes:\n\n\tq[0,t]   \[Alpha]  - ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x"], 
    RowBox[{"(", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "[", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", "t"}], "]"}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"d620a58a-2eb3-4fe4-9629-e5e8bde2cc74"],
 "\t\n\tq[L,t]   \[Alpha]  - ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x"], 
    RowBox[{"(", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "[", 
      RowBox[{"L", ",", "t"}], "]"}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"74f05686-8961-4da3-90bd-634bb041e3ac"],
 "\n\t\nRemember, flux moves in the opposite direction of increasing density.\
\nThus, if we equate condition \"1\" and \"2\", then the boundary conditions \
become:\n\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x"], 
    RowBox[{"(", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "[", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", "t"}], "]"}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"513781c4-5ed0-43a6-9e7f-fd9376a98c9d"],
 "  =  \[Mu]0 \[Rho][0,t]\t (the flux out is right to left)\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x"], 
    RowBox[{"(", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "[", 
      RowBox[{"L", ",", "t"}], "]"}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"55cb86a7-ddf7-46ef-b5ba-a6b250cf00a7"],
 "  =  - \[Mu]L \[Rho][L,t]\t (the flux out is left to right)\n\nThe \
constants of proportionality \[Mu]0 and \[Mu]L are determined from the \
physics of the process.\n\nIf we try to solve the steady state ODE with these \
boundary conditions, Mathematica will only return the zero solution (which is \
correct).  "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.7504245524304223`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"3ab335e2-ab76-4a5a-b095-\
dad20e439cba"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"DSolve", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"\[Nu]", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         SuperscriptBox[
          SuperscriptBox["\[Rho]", "\[Prime]",
           MultilineFunction->None], "\[Prime]",
          MultilineFunction->None], "[", "x", "]"}]}], "+", 
       RowBox[{"r", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "[", "x", "]"}]}]}], "\[Equal]", "0"}], ",", 
     "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox["\[Rho]", "\[Prime]",
        MultilineFunction->None], "[", "0", "]"}], "\[Equal]", 
      RowBox[{"\[Mu]0", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "[", "0", "]"}]}]}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox["\[Rho]", "\[Prime]",
        MultilineFunction->None], "[", "L", "]"}], "\[Equal]", 
      RowBox[{"\[Mu]L", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "[", 
        RowBox[{"0", "L"}], "]"}]}]}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", "}"}], ",", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "[", "x", "]"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", "x"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]",
   "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3984943804309998`*^9, 3.398494399292*^9}, {
  3.7504244595821385`*^9, 3.7504245027904587`*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1484]:=",ExpressionUUID->"0d837ae1-efbb-4e9f-9455-ae08c8e9d839"],

Cell["\<\
Therefore, as above, we will apply just one boundary condition:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.750424571480327*^9},ExpressionUUID->"4d135f70-59e7-4af6-8702-\
fc4976168015"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"DSolve", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"\[Nu]", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         SuperscriptBox[
          SuperscriptBox["\[Rho]", "\[Prime]",
           MultilineFunction->None], "\[Prime]",
          MultilineFunction->None], "[", "x", "]"}]}], "+", 
       RowBox[{"r", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "[", "x", "]"}]}]}], "\[Equal]", "0"}], ",", 
     "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox["\[Rho]", "\[Prime]",
        MultilineFunction->None], "[", "0", "]"}], "\[Equal]", 
      RowBox[{"\[Mu]0", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "[", "0", "]"}]}]}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", "}"}], 
   ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "[", "x", "]"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", "x"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]",
   "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3984943804309998`*^9, 3.398494399292*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1485]:=",ExpressionUUID->"8ae38482-cc10-4c42-8535-ae341ae841a1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{" ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
    "Solve", " ", "for", " ", "the", " ", "value", " ", "of", " ", "L", " ", 
     "which", " ", "satisfies", " ", "the", " ", "second", " ", "boundary", 
     " ", 
     RowBox[{"condition", ":", "\n", "\n", "\t\t", 
      RowBox[{"Solve", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x"], 
          RowBox[{"(", " ", 
           RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "[", 
            RowBox[{"L", ",", "t"}], "]"}], ")"}]}], "  ", "=", "  ", 
         RowBox[{"\[Mu]L", " ", 
          RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "[", 
           RowBox[{"L", ",", "t"}], "]"}]}]}], ",", "  ", "L"}], "]"}]}]}], 
    "\n", "\t"}]}], TextForm]], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"83e61183-f9b8-4acd-\
b8cc-e16d8c4134d0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"solnRules", "=", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{"Solve", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x"], 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"C", "[", "2", "]"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
          FractionBox[
           RowBox[{
            SqrtBox["r"], " ", "x"}], 
           SqrtBox["\[Nu]"]], "]"}]}], "+", 
        FractionBox[
         RowBox[{"\[Mu]0", " ", 
          SqrtBox["\[Nu]"], " ", 
          RowBox[{"C", "[", "2", "]"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
           FractionBox[
            RowBox[{
             SqrtBox["r"], " ", "x"}], 
            SqrtBox["\[Nu]"]], "]"}]}], 
         SqrtBox["r"]]}], ")"}]}], "\[Equal]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "\[Mu]L"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"C", "[", "2", "]"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
          FractionBox[
           RowBox[{
            SqrtBox["r"], " ", "x"}], 
           SqrtBox["\[Nu]"]], "]"}]}], "+", 
        FractionBox[
         RowBox[{"\[Mu]0", " ", 
          SqrtBox["\[Nu]"], " ", 
          RowBox[{"C", "[", "2", "]"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
           FractionBox[
            RowBox[{
             SqrtBox["r"], " ", "x"}], 
            SqrtBox["\[Nu]"]], "]"}]}], 
         SqrtBox["r"]]}], ")"}]}]}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", "x"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.398494416973*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1486]:=",ExpressionUUID->"2f30f38c-ec9b-4163-9ba2-abddf3b862e4"],

Cell["\<\
Presumably one of the ArcCos values would correspond to the smallest value of \
L corresponding to the steady state solution with flux boundary conditions.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"58084f4d-3e32-4720-92bb-53454a40f0f3"],

Cell["\<\
Consider some numeric values (precise values would depend upon measurements \
specific to plankton blooms):\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"247c3054-9a3b-4584-9f36-a69c0f41182f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"x", "  ", "/.", " ", "solnRules"}], " ", "/.", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[Mu]0", "\[Rule]", ".10"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\[Mu]L", "\[Rule]", ".10"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"\[Nu]", "  ", "\[Rule]", "  ", "1"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"r", "  ", "\[Rule]", "  ", ".1"}]}], "}"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1487]:=",ExpressionUUID->"14888b9c-5774-4e89-878c-d6f0c3313523"],

Cell["\<\
Further analysis would be required to determine the significance of the above \
values.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"66d43179-3f0e-445c-846a-b54c428efbf5"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
 Non-equilibrium solutions (with fixed boundary conditions):
\
\>", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.4651514743972025`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"7f758ae6-43f0-41b0-81d9-\
2315cb585a21"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Some of the more interesting behavior of our model would correspond to \
non-equilibrium solutions.  However, the complexity of the solutions for the \
PDE necessitate the use of numerical methods.  Therefore, specific values \
corresponding to the physical process will be assigned:\n\n \t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{" ", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "t"], 
     RowBox[{"(", " ", "\[Rho]", " ", ")"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"28e3c82e-8b38-4712-a7f2-be247a263ece"],
 "  =   \[Nu] ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{" ", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "xx"], 
     RowBox[{"(", " ", 
      FormBox[
       RowBox[{"\[Rho]", ")"}],
       TraditionalForm], " "}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "f9f4b65e-275b-445f-9041-157a80dabd28"],
 "  +  r \[Rho]\n \t\n \t\[Rho][x,0]  =  x*(10-x)\n \t\[Rho][0,t]  =  0\t \
(Use the 0 density boundary conditions)\n\t\[Rho][L,t]  =  0\t (Use the 0 \
density boundary conditions)\n\t\n\tL  =  10\n\ttStop = 50\n\t\[Nu]  =  1\n\t\
r  =  .02\n\t"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.39849445425*^9},ExpressionUUID->"a0d9aac7-70c1-4d23-b068-a06f3d07ce94"],

Cell["\<\
The initial density distribution of the plankton is assumed to be:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8bb7103d-957e-416d-b373-1643dea8be84"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Plot", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"x", "*", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"10", "-", "x"}], ")"}]}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"x", ",", "0", ",", "10"}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"AxesLabel", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<x\>\"", ",", "\"\<\[Rho]\>\""}], "}"}]}]}], 
  "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3984944727939997`*^9, 3.398494500802*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1488]:=",ExpressionUUID->"a6b66a8a-ab9b-4da5-b15e-deef9a0b2e3a"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"L", "  ", "=", "  ", "10"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[Nu]", "  ", "=", " ", "1"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"r", "  ", "=", "  ", ".02"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"tStop", " ", "=", " ", "50"}], ";"}]}], "InputOnly",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.465151662950229*^9, 3.465151665685147*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1489]:=",ExpressionUUID->"43777287-1cf9-458e-a199-dbc40b68abfb"],

Cell["The numerical solution for these conditions is:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0056a3b5-511e-4c43-82b8-9cee551e9624"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"solutionRule", "=", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"NDSolve", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "t"], 
         RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "[", 
          RowBox[{"x", ",", "t"}], "]"}]}], "\[Equal]", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"\[Nu]", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", 
            RowBox[{"x", ",", "x"}]], 
           RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "[", 
            RowBox[{"x", ",", "t"}], "]"}]}]}], "+", 
         RowBox[{"r", " ", 
          RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "[", 
           RowBox[{"x", ",", "t"}], "]"}]}]}]}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
       "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "[", 
         RowBox[{"x", ",", "0"}], "]"}], "\[Equal]", 
        RowBox[{"x", " ", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"10", "-", "x"}], ")"}]}]}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "[", 
         RowBox[{"0", ",", "t"}], "]"}], "\[Equal]", "0"}], ",", 
       "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "[", 
         RowBox[{"L", ",", "t"}], "]"}], "\[Equal]", "0"}]}], 
      "\[IndentingNewLine]", "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[Rho]", ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"x", ",", "0", ",", "L"}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"t", ",", "0", ",", "tStop"}], "}"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398494518553*^9, 3.398494572066*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1493]:=",ExpressionUUID->"2a6e7b63-e712-45c5-b5a4-bb4308ed25ee"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Plot3D", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "[", 
     RowBox[{"x", ",", "t"}], "]"}], "/.", "\[InvisibleSpace]", 
    RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", "solutionRule", "]"}]}], ",", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"x", ",", "0", ",", "L"}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"t", ",", "0", ",", "tStop"}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"AxesLabel", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<x\>\"", ",", "\"\<t\>\"", ",", "\"\<\[Rho]\>\""}], 
     "}"}]}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.398494584888*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1494]:=",ExpressionUUID->"4179a2b7-3a12-46b2-afce-7e5d2b16a748"],

Cell["\<\
We can see from the above plot that the diffusion exceeds the increase in \
population due to reproduction.  For these specific values the algae bloom \
will die out.

One possible solution to insure the survival is to increase the reproductive \
rate (for the following example by a factor of 5):\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"78e9e064-636d-41a5-b518-a33481226800"],

Cell["\<\
\tL  =  10
\ttStop = 50
\t\[Nu]  =  1
\tr  =  .1\t\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cef1ccc6-731f-48ca-a9fd-d03db4f15509"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"L", "  ", "=", "  ", "10"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[Nu]", "  ", "=", " ", "1"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"r", "  ", "=", "  ", ".1"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"tStop", " ", "=", " ", "50"}], ";"}]}], "InputOnly",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.465151681703949*^9, 3.4651516839231396`*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1495]:=",ExpressionUUID->"1fa9a00d-ed4b-4ff8-a02b-a7cf7f9bdfaf"],

