 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3984969321879997`*^9, 3.398496935855*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1545]:=",ExpressionUUID->"74502639-145f-4977-b9ea-529993aa726d"],

Cell["\<\
We can see from the above plot that the reproductive rate is slightly higher \
than the diffusion rate.  For these specific values the algae bloom will \
grow.
By increasing the time interval it is possible to show that this problem will \
approach a steady state solution as well.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8365c8ed-e0f2-4cc6-b63e-5ff71cbdf1d1"],

Cell["\<\

As a final consideration, what will happen if we start out with a density \
distribution which exceeds the maximum carrying capacity (i.e. k)?  We have \
shown above that steady state equilibrium solutions cannot exist for such a \
density distribution.  In the example that follows, the initial density \
distribution is increased by a factor of 7.  It therefore exceeds the maximum \
carrying capacity at the midpoint.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fa4f2934-db17-4d0f-8fb9-4d5e29b93d48"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Plot", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"7", "*", "x", "*", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"10", "-", "x"}], ")"}]}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"x", ",", "0", ",", "10"}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"AxesLabel", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<x\>\"", ",", "\"\<\[Rho]\>\""}], "}"}]}]}], 
  "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.39849695225*^9, 3.398496963106*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1546]:=",ExpressionUUID->"4bda16ed-b8ef-48fa-bfe8-dd0d4e208d2e"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"L", "  ", "=", "  ", "10"}], ";"}], "\n", 
